+## Finding under disposition
+`balanced-fj-sufficiency-alln`, #301 comment 2026-11-21T17:30:30.538Z. Defines
+C(n)=ceil(log2 n!), F(m)=sum_{k=1}^m ceil(log2(3k/4)) (Ford-Johnson upper bound),
+a=floor(n/2), b=ceil(n/2). Claim P: C(n) >= F(a)+F(b)+a+1 for every n>=3.
+Consequence: S(n) >= S(floor(n/2)) + S(ceil(n/2)) + floor(n/2) + 1 for all n>=3.
+This would extend the earlier 16:42Z finite-range antichain defect theorem
+(certified only for a+b<=50) to ALL balanced splits of every size.
